# uv, the installer Columbus runs to create the environments the person
# approves (propose_environment, build brief Part 5).
# This is the source: requirements-uv.txt is generated from it, pinned by
# version and by the SHA-256 of every wheel. Edit this file, then run
#   python packaging/engine/compile-requirements.py
# Install the .txt into the engine on its own, so every wheel is checked and
# nothing else is pulled in:
#
#   python -m pip install --require-hashes --no-deps --only-binary :all: -r workers/python/requirements-uv.txt
#
# Columbus finds it inside the engine (uv.find_uv_bin()), never on PATH.
# uv is MIT OR Apache-2.0 (Astral); its licence files are in the wheel.
